<title>SPAIN: Spain's Uralita sells Duraval unit.</title>
<headline>Spain's Uralita sells Duraval unit.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish building materials group Uralita  said on Friday it had sold its unit Duraval to NatWest Ventures and  Electra Fleming for 2.0 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>It said Duraval had annual turnover of 3.0 million pesetas in sales  of paint and varnishes.</p>
<p>Uralita said in a statement the sale was part of a strategy to concentrate  on business in construction materials with potential for international  growth.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom + 34 1 585-8341</p>
</text>
